/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  aniline-tetrahydropyran -- AN NRTL PAIR FROM EVERY LABORATORY'S BUBBLE PRESSURES.

  WRITTEN BY bin/curate/pairs_px.py (DEV.md 4c C291, the P-x mirror of the
  C284 bubble-temperature pipeline; record
  docs/design/binary-pairs-from-open-measurements.md section 12).

  THE DECLARATION -- WRITTEN AND COMMITTED BEFORE ANY FIT RAN (several
  declarations of a batch share one commit).

  IDENTITY.  aniline (CAS 62-53-3, InChIKey PAYRUJLWNCNPSJ-UHFFFAOYSA-N)
  + tetrahydropyran (CAS 142-68-7, InChIKey DHXVGJBLRPWPCS-UHFFFAOYSA-N), joined
  to the archive through identity.json -- never by name.  CLASS (C284): both
  records are volatile molecular liquids (no role nonvolatile/solute, no
  dissociatesTo, no charge, no solid, a vapour-pressure model), and every
  measured temperature lies below both critical temperatures.

  NO MEASURED SERIES IN THIS TREE.  constant/archiveDatasets names each
  dataset (DOI, NIST URL, article sha256, extraction selector, extract
  sha256); `bin/choupo-curate fetch` writes the points into
  constant/archiveExtracts/, which is gitignored.

  STUDIES: every isothermal bubble-pressure block of the pair at or below
  110 kPa that states an uncertainty on every point.  FITTED, ALL OF THEM
  (1 block(s), 1 laboratory(ies), 1 temperature(s)):
      10.1021/je1005196              block 17   10 pts  308.15 K  0.56-12.8256 kPa  U 0.11066-0.44 kPa
  SET ASIDE BY THE EXTRACTION RULES, BY NAME:
      (none)

  THE RULE (DEV.md 4c C291, bubble-pressure pairs).  Every block above is
  fitted together; none is held out.  NRTL, a_ij = a_ji = 0, alpha = 0.30
  fixed: two parameters (b_ij, b_ji), so tau = b/T carries the temperature
  dependence.  The residual is the bubble PRESSURE at each point's stated
  temperature, RELATIVE, (P_model - P)/P; objective twoStage (least squares,
  then minimax; P_bubble relative).  OUTLIERS: after a least-squares stage over
  every point, a point with |P_model - P|/P > 20 % is discarded BY NAME
  (`discard` on its evidence entry, listed below) and the fit repeated
  without it; a STUDY with more than half of its points beyond 20 % is
  discarded whole, by name (it contradicts the model and the other
  laboratories as a whole, e.g. a composition labelled as the other member's).
  THE GRADED ACCEPTANCE (DEV.md 4c C285, in per cent of P): max |P_model - P|/P over the KEPT points is GRADED -- clean up to 5 %, warning up to 10 %, severe up to 20 %, refused above; a point with no bubble pressure refuses.  Every grade but refused is accepted and promoted (autoPromoted, humanReviewed false) with `fitGrade` and its max relative error in the record's provenance; the engine voices a warning or a severe grade on every run that reads the pair.  A pair that splits ONE liquid inside its validity span is not promoted, whatever its grade (arm f).
  Two starts: (0, 0) and (800, -400).  The per-point uncertainty U (kPa) is
  kept in each dataset and is information: this residual is already relative.

  OUTLIERS DISCARDED AFTER THE LEAST-SQUARES STAGE:
  @@OUTLIERS-BEGIN@@
      1 point(s) of 10: doi 10.1021/je1005196 row 10: x 0.9502, T 308.15
      K, P 0.560 kPa, the model finds no bubble pressure
  @@OUTLIERS-END@@

  @@MODELS-BEGIN@@
  THE OTHER ACTIVITY MODELS (DEV.md 4c C294), declared before their fits
  ran. The SAME datasets and the SAME kept points as fit_nrtl: each op
  below is fit_nrtl copied verbatim -- evidence, discards, objective,
  residual, weighting, options -- with only its parameters, its `thermo
  {}` fragment (the model) and its outputs changed; the outlier discard
  was decided ONCE, on the NRTL least-squares stage, and is reused, never
  re-decided per model. UNIQUAC: two parameters a_ij, a_ji (K), tau_ij =
  exp(-a_ij/T), b = c = 0 fixed (the NRTL default's count; temperature
  dependence 1/T), r and q each component's own record. Wilson: two
  parameters A_ij, A_ji (J/mol), Lambda_ij = (V_j/V_i) exp(-A_ij/RT), V
  the records' Vliq. Two starts each. Each model gets its own record
  (constant/parameters/<MODEL>/), its own grade at 5 / 10 / 20 % (max
  |P_model - P|/P), its own one-liquid test (arm f), `fitGradeBasis
  inSample`, the C300 cap and `review { by none; }`; a severe or refused
  grade, or a split, is not promoted. The three in-sample residuals are
  published side by side, never used to choose a model for the student.
  UNIQUAC: NOT FITTED -- aniline and tetrahydropyran carry no UNIQUAC r
  and q (no tabulated value, and no UNIFAC groups to sum them from,
  bin/curate/uniquac_rq_from_groups.py) -- UNIQUAC is not fitted; nothing
  is estimated silently. Wilson: FITTED.
  @@MODELS-END@@

  @@MODELS-RESULT-BEGIN@@
  WHAT THE UNIQUAC AND WILSON FITS FOUND (pinned in `expected`; measured,
  not argued). Beside fit_nrtl's max |dP|/P 9.000 % (warning) on the same
  kept points. fit_wilson: A_ij = 3832.8, A_ji = -3832.7 J/mol over 9
  kept points: max |dP|/P 8.474 %, mean 5.384 %, graded warning ->
  accepted; fit_wilson_start2 lands on the same pair (3831.0, -3832.3).
  PROMOTED on 2026-11-11 into
  data/standards/parameters/Wilson/aniline-tetrahydropyran.dat as
  reviewStatus autoPromoted, review by none, because: fit grade warning
  -- max |dP|/P 8.474 % over the 9 kept points, one liquid across the
  validity span. UNIQUAC: not fitted -- aniline and tetrahydropyran carry
  no UNIQUAC r and q (no tabulated value, and no UNIFAC groups to sum
  them from, bin/curate/uniquac_rq_from_groups.py) -- UNIQUAC is not
  fitted; nothing is estimated silently.
  @@MODELS-RESULT-END@@

  @@RESULT-BEGIN@@
  WHAT THE RUN FOUND (pinned in `expected`; measured, not argued).
  fit_nrtl: b_ij = -521.0 K, b_ji = 439.9 K over 9 kept points of 1
  block(s), 1 laboratory(ies), 1 temperature(s) (1 discarded): max |dP|/P
  9.00 %, mean 4.78 %, graded warning -> accepted. fit_nrtl_start2 lands
  on A DIFFERENT pair (1371.2, -625.9). PROMOTED on 2026-11-11 into
  data/standards/parameters/NRTL/aniline-tetrahydropyran.dat as
  reviewStatus autoPromoted, review by none, because: fit grade warning
  -- max |dP|/P 9.00 % over the 9 kept points (limits 5 / 10 / 20 %), one
  liquid across the validity span SINGLE TEMPERATURE: b/T was fitted at
  one temperature; its extrapolation is untested. SINGLE LABORATORY: one
  article's data, nothing to cross-check it.
  @@RESULT-END@@

  WHAT IS NOT CLAIMED.  The pair is correct at these temperatures in this
  frame (ideal-gas vapour, the catalogue's own vapour-pressure records); the
  measurements were transcribed by the archive and have NOT been read back
  against the articles (the CHECKLIST that `fetch` writes is the aid).
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

operations
(
    {
        name        fit_nrtl;
        type        fitParameters;

        parameters
        (
            { path  equilibrium.liquid.activityModel.binaryParameters.aniline-tetrahydropyran.b_ij;  initial 0;  min -3000;  max 3000; }
            { path  equilibrium.liquid.activityModel.binaryParameters.aniline-tetrahydropyran.b_ji;  initial 0;  min -3000;  max 3000; }
        );

        evidence
        (
            {
                dataset  "constant/archiveExtracts/aniline-tetrahydropyran-bubbleP-je1005196-b17.dat";
                role     fit;
                discard  ( 10 );   // C291 outliers, by name in the header
            }
        );

        objective { method twoStage;  scale { P_bubble relative; } }
        residual
        {
            kind        P_bubble;
            components  ( aniline tetrahydropyran );
        }

        options
        {
            maxIter      80;
            tolerance    1.0e-6;
            fdStep       1.0e-4;
            lambda0      1.0e-3;
        }

        output
        {
            fit_log    fit_history.csv;
            parity     parity.csv;
            proposal   aniline-tetrahydropyran.proposal.dat;
        }
    }
    {
        name        fit_nrtl_start2;
        type        fitParameters;

        parameters
        (
            { path  equilibrium.liquid.activityModel.binaryParameters.aniline-tetrahydropyran.b_ij;  initial 800;  min -3000;  max 3000; }
            { path  equilibrium.liquid.activityModel.binaryParameters.aniline-tetrahydropyran.b_ji;  initial -400;  min -3000;  max 3000; }
        );

        evidence
        (
            {
                dataset  "constant/archiveExtracts/aniline-tetrahydropyran-bubbleP-je1005196-b17.dat";
                role     fit;
                discard  ( 10 );   // C291 outliers, by name in the header
            }
        );

        objective { method twoStage;  scale { P_bubble relative; } }
        residual
        {
            kind        P_bubble;
            components  ( aniline tetrahydropyran );
        }

        options
        {
            maxIter      80;
            tolerance    1.0e-6;
            fdStep       1.0e-4;
            lambda0      1.0e-3;
        }

        output
        {
            parity     parity_start2.csv;
        }
    }
    {
        name        txy_nrtl;
        type        propertyScan1D;
        vary        { variable x[aniline];  from 0.0;  to 1.0;  n 101; }
        state       { P 6.5995 kPa;  composition { aniline 0.5;  tetrahydropyran 0.5; } }
        thermo
        {
            equilibrium { liquid { activityModel { model NRTL; /* no inline pair: the case's own record */ } } }
        }
        properties  ( T_bubble  y_eq_aniline );
        output      { file txy_nrtl.csv; }
    }
    // @@C294-OPS-BEGIN@@ -- UNIQUAC and Wilson on the NRTL fit's own evidence (DEV.md 4c C294)
    {
        name        fit_wilson;
        type        fitParameters;

        parameters
        (
            { path  equilibrium.liquid.activityModel.binaryParameters.aniline-tetrahydropyran.A_ij;  initial 0;  min -30000;  max 30000; }
            { path  equilibrium.liquid.activityModel.binaryParameters.aniline-tetrahydropyran.A_ji;  initial 0;  min -30000;  max 30000; }
        );

        thermo   // the model, as a fragment of the case's system (C294)
        {
            equilibrium
            {
                liquid
                {
                    activityModel
                    {
                        model Wilson;
                        binaryParameters   // the FIT'S starting point
                        {
                            aniline-tetrahydropyran { i aniline; j tetrahydropyran; A_ij 0; A_ji 0; }
                        }
                    }
                    standardState pureLiquid;
                }
            }
        }

        evidence
        (
            {
                dataset  "constant/archiveExtracts/aniline-tetrahydropyran-bubbleP-je1005196-b17.dat";
                role     fit;
                discard  ( 10 );   // the NRTL fit's outliers, reused: decided once (C294)
            }
        );

        objective { method twoStage;  scale { P_bubble relative; } }
        residual
        {
            kind        P_bubble;
            components  ( aniline tetrahydropyran );
        }

        options
        {
            maxIter      80;
            tolerance    1.0e-6;
            fdStep       1.0e-4;
            lambda0      1.0e-3;
        }

        output
        {
            fit_log    fit_history_wilson.csv;
            parity     parity_wilson.csv;
            proposal   aniline-tetrahydropyran.Wilson.proposal.dat;
        }
    }
    {
        name        fit_wilson_start2;
        type        fitParameters;

        parameters
        (
            { path  equilibrium.liquid.activityModel.binaryParameters.aniline-tetrahydropyran.A_ij;  initial 4000;  min -30000;  max 30000; }
            { path  equilibrium.liquid.activityModel.binaryParameters.aniline-tetrahydropyran.A_ji;  initial -2000;  min -30000;  max 30000; }
        );

        thermo   // the model, as a fragment of the case's system (C294)
        {
            equilibrium
            {
                liquid
                {
                    activityModel
                    {
                        model Wilson;
                        binaryParameters   // the FIT'S starting point
                        {
                            aniline-tetrahydropyran { i aniline; j tetrahydropyran; A_ij 0; A_ji 0; }
                        }
                    }
                    standardState pureLiquid;
                }
            }
        }

        evidence
        (
            {
                dataset  "constant/archiveExtracts/aniline-tetrahydropyran-bubbleP-je1005196-b17.dat";
                role     fit;
                discard  ( 10 );   // the NRTL fit's outliers, reused: decided once (C294)
            }
        );

        objective { method twoStage;  scale { P_bubble relative; } }
        residual
        {
            kind        P_bubble;
            components  ( aniline tetrahydropyran );
        }

        options
        {
            maxIter      80;
            tolerance    1.0e-6;
            fdStep       1.0e-4;
            lambda0      1.0e-3;
        }

        output
        {
            parity     parity_wilson_start2.csv;
        }
    }
    // @@C294-OPS-END@@
    // @@C294-READBACK-BEGIN@@ -- each model's record, read as the catalogue reads it
    {
        name        txy_wilson;
        type        propertyScan1D;
        vary        { variable x[aniline];  from 0.0;  to 1.0;  n 101; }
        state       { P 6.5995 kPa;  composition { aniline 0.5;  tetrahydropyran 0.5; } }
        thermo
        {
            equilibrium { liquid { activityModel { model Wilson; /* no inline pair: the case's own record */ } } }
        }
        properties  ( T_bubble  y_eq_aniline );
        output      { file txy_wilson.csv; }
    }
    // @@C294-READBACK-END@@
);
